;; M4S multi-constructor support (docs/m4s-contract.md, required fixtures):
;; identical struct content constructed by TWO rules.  With a = b = {7}:
;;   out (mk 7) -> (input 0, nonrec 2, rec 0)   one row, two constructors
;;   mk  (mk 7) -> (input 0, nonrec 2, rec 0)   one interned instance
;; Deleting a(7) is a support-only decrement (the row stays live on the b
;; constructor, nonrec 2 -> 1, SAME id); deleting b(7) as well tombstones
;; it (0 live, 1 tombstone).
;;
;; The same program serves the mixed-sign-epoch fixture: from a = {7},
;; b = {}, one flush {-a(7), +b(7)} kills and revives (mk 7) inside a
;; single update epoch -- the id must survive (within-epoch resurrection,
;; M5).

table (a int)
table (b int)
struct (mk int)
table (out mk)

rule
(a X)
-->
(out (mk X))

rule
(b X)
-->
(out (mk X))
